{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 formalization of the paper 'Powers of a Prime in the Image of Summatory Valuation Functions', on the question of Nicolas about the powers of 2 in the image of c(n) = sum_{k=1}^{n} 2^{v_2(k)}. It proves the recurrences and the binary formula for c, the equivalence of Theorem thm:equiv, the greedy lemma, the leading term and the recursion on states with its algorithm, the explicit members and non-members, the one-step classification, the families of Nicolas and their counting, the lower bounds for the counting functions A(x) and B(x) (Theorems thm:counting and thm:counting2), the forest of successful states, the bottom-up recursion and the symmetry, the further families of Theorem thm:symfamilies, and the analogue for an arbitrary prime p (Lemma lem:cp, Proposition prop:Fp, Theorems thm:primes, thm:primestep, thm:primefamilies, thm:immediate, thm:primebottomup and Proposition prop:primezero). Everything is proved from Mathlib. The worked numerical examples of the text and the computations of Section sec:experiments are not formalized.",
